{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinhtrung/fleet-console/pulls/14","id":5054837244,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVYupSs8AAAABLUqx_A","html_url":"https://github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/pull/14","diff_url":"https://github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/pull/14.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/pull/14.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinhtrung/fleet-console/issues/14","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinhtrung/fleet-console/pulls/14/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinhtrung/fleet-console/pulls/14/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinhtrung/fleet-console/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinhtrung/fleet-console/issues/14/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dinhtrung/fleet-console/statuses/a21e0626300f54f2c062bbb8026fe67bbdf47c3d","number":14,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(decide): port dispatcher rules and add the golden oracle (#3)","user":{"login":"dinhtrung","id":137198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzE5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung","html_url":"https://github.com/dinhtrung","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Port the dispatcher rules and build the golden oracle\n\nCloses #3\n\n## What\n\n`internal/decide` now holds the dispatcher's rules as pure functions over a snapshot\n(`Decide(Snapshot) Result`), ported from `~/bin/fleet-autodispatch.py` without changing a rule:\n\n- epic skip, parent gate (child of an open epic only), `onhold` on the task or its parent,\n  live-row-body idempotency, branch-on-origin (open CR blocks, merged CR is a marker leak,\n  a branch with no CR is adopted), one-way blocking (GitLab smaller-number `related`; GitHub\n  native `blocked_by`), ascending order, and the free-builder / `concurrency_cap` cap.\n- Every candidate carries a `Reason`; a candidate with neither a dispatch nor a reason fails\n  `TestOracle`. A failed forge read returns `stale`, never `nothing`.\n- Order and precedence match the Python loop: dispatched → live row → branch → blockers.\n\nThe oracle: `scripts/record-decide-ticks.py` projects the decision-relevant inputs of real\ndispatcher ticks out of `~/logs/fleet-autodispatch.log`, replays each one through the actual\nPython `main()` with its reads frozen to the snapshot (no side effects, `--apply` off), and\nonly keeps ticks where the replay reproduces the recorded outcome. `go test ./internal/decide\n-run TestOracle` replays the recording through the Go plan and diffs the task set and reasons.\n\nFiles: `internal/decide/decide.go`, `decide_test.go`, `oracle_test.go`, 20 tick directories\nunder `internal/decide/testdata/ticks/`, `scripts/record-decide-ticks.py`; tasks 1.4 and 1.5\nare ticked in `openspec/changes/fleet-console-v1/tasks.md`.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [x] One table test per rule, named after the rule: `TestRuleEpicSkipped`, `TestRuleParentGate`,\n      `TestRuleOnHoldCascade`, `TestRuleLiveRowIdempotency`, `TestRuleBranchOnOrigin`,\n      `TestRuleOneWayBlockingGitLab`, `TestRuleOneWayBlockingGitHub`, `TestRuleAscendingOrder`,\n      `TestRuleCapByFreeBuilders`, `TestRuleBusyBuilder`.\n- [x] `go test ./internal/decide -run TestOracle` green over 20 recorded ticks (28 dispatched\n      tasks across them; reason coverage: epic 166, blocked 65, live_row 15, no_free_builder 11,\n      onhold 10, parent_onhold 6, branch_open_cr 2).\n- [x] Killing the forge read yields `stale`, not \"no tasks\": `TestForgeReadStale`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nOracle diff is empty — all 20 subtests pass:\n\n```text\n$ go test ./internal/decide -run TestOracle -count=1 -v\n--- PASS: TestOracle (0.00s)\n    --- PASS: TestOracle/tick-01-202610232254120700 (0.00s)\n    ...\n    --- PASS: TestOracle/tick-20-202610262249100700 (0.00s)\nPASS\n```\n\nThe oracle is not tautological: flipping the GitLab rule from `link.Number < item.Number` to\n`>` makes it fail (`dispatches = [85 86 87], want [85 86 103]` on three ticks); reverted.\n\nRecording: 259 ticks replay-verified, 379 candidate ticks rejected (projection mismatch or\nact-time failure in the log), 20 selected. Each tick's `provenance.txt` carries the log lines\nit was recorded from and `Replay-verified ...: True`.\n\nOne tick's pair — `tick-10-202610222355100700`:\n\n```text\n# inputs (snapshot.json, decision-relevant projection)\nopen epics [101, 102, 111]; open tasks [109, 110]; free=3\n110 relates_to 109 (both open); no rows, no branches\n# Python dispatcher output at 2026-10-22T23:55:10+0700\n#110 skip: blocked by open #109\nready: [109]\n#109 dispatched\n```\n```json\n{\"status\":\"planned\",\"dispatches\":[109],\n \"reasons\":{\"101\":\"epic\",\"102\":\"epic\",\"111\":\"epic\",\"110\":\"blocked\"}}\n```\n\n## Commands and real output\n\n```text\n$ go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test ./...\n?    github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/cmd/fleet-console   [no test files]\n?    github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/internal/act       [no test files]\nok   github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/internal/decide\n?    github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/internal/forge     [no test files]\n?    github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/internal/git       [no test files]\nok   github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/internal/rig\nok   github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/internal/store\nok   github.com/dinhtrung/fleet-console/internal/web\nexit=0\n\n$ CGO_ENABLED=0 go build ./...\nexit=0\n\n$ openspec validate --all --strict\n✓ change/fleet-console-v1\n✓ change/stack-provisioning\nTotals: 2 passed, 0 failed (2 items)\n\n$ npm ci && npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run build\nexit=0\n```\n\n## Limits\n\n- The ticks are real dispatcher ticks, but their snapshots are the decision-relevant projection\n  of the log (the rules read only items, links, branches, rows, seats and the limit), not a\n  byte-for-byte mirror of the GitLab API. `provenance.txt` keeps the original lines, and the\n  replay check rejects any projection that does not reproduce the Python outcome.\n- `branch_merged_cr` is covered by the table test only; no verified tick carried a merged-CR\n  warning. The GitHub native `blocked_by` path is likewise table-tested; the recorded ticks are\n  GitLab ticks because the named contract is the GitLab dispatcher.\n- Housekeeping and the merge watchdog are out of tasks 1.4/1.5 and are not ported here.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T17:28:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T17:39:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"dinhtrung:feature/3-p0-port-the-dispatcher-rules","ref":"feature/3-p0-port-the-dispatcher-rules","repo":{"id":1435216202,"node_id":"R_kgDOVYupSg","name":"fleet-console","full_name":"dinhtrung/fleet-console","owner":{"login":"dinhtrung","id":137198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzE5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung","html_url":"https://github.com/dinhtrung","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dinhtrung/following{/othe